  "narrative": "These triple-stratum analyses strongly resolve the dependence structure among the three leading binary predictors. The feature_037 association is not a proxy for feature_010 or feature_003: in feature_010-negative/feature_003-negative individuals (H73), in feature_010-positive/feature_003-negative individuals (H74), and in feature_010-negative/feature_003-positive individuals (H75), the signed estimates are 0.845, 0.803, and 0.782, with 95% intervals entirely far above the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept these as precise dataset-specific conditional associations and close the exact claims. Reciprocally, feature_003 and feature_010 are not fully explained by feature_037. Feature_003 positivity is associated with a lower score by 0.481 units among feature_037-negative individuals with high feature_036 (H78), well above threshold; this is a key refinement of the validated high-feature_036 effect and I request validation for it. Feature_010 positivity is associated with a higher score by 0.440 units among feature_037-negative/feature_003-negative individuals (H79), by 0.483 units among feature_037-positive/feature_003-negative individuals (H80), and by 0.606 units among feature_037-negative/high-feature_036 individuals (H81); all intervals clear the threshold, so I accept these dataset-specific conditional associations. The direct feature_003 association in feature_037-negative/feature_010-negative individuals is directionally stable but only 0.135 units (H76), below threshold with an interval crossing 0.15; I defer it rather than accept a threshold-scale claim. The analogous feature_003 association among feature_037-negative/feature_010-positive individuals is imprecise (H77), so it remains deferred. For standardized-signature modification, H82 provides no threshold evidence that the feature_037 association is stronger in high feature_038; I reject and close that direction. H83 is near threshold (0.156) but its interval extends well below threshold, so I defer it rather than claim meaningful modification. The most notable opposite result is H84: under the registered positive feature_010 interaction direction, the signed estimate is -0.559 with an interval entirely beyond threshold in the opposite direction. I therefore reject H84 as registered, but register a reversed interaction claim because this is strong evidence that the feature_010 association differs substantially across high feature_038. All conclusions are unadjusted dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
